notes               = "Untitled in source. Source includes a polished human translation (kept in the translation section); imported as a draft per instruction — flip draft to false to render it. The machine section holds the raw MT shown in the Drafts tab. Merged (July 2026) with `rain-memory`, a duplicate of this poem created by the pages 61-69 bulk import, which did not dedupe against the file already in the repo. The agent rendering the older file had staged in ===translation=== is withdrawn from that slot, which is Ben's; the page-73 lantern stands. Both files were agent-made, so there is no Ben layer here to protect: this is a merge of an import from the Adobe dump with a conversion of the page-73 photograph transcription. The page number, Persian, machine pass and lantern come from the page-73 side. The two sources disagreed on the first word — the dump read های... باران... ('hey... rain...') and the transcription های... یاران... ('hey... friends...'), one letter apart. Ben checked page 73: it is باران, rain, so the dump had it right and the transcription is corrected. The Persian, machine pass and lantern here follow, and the addressee shift this note used to flag is gone with it: the poem speaks to the rain throughout."
draft               = true

===persian===

های... باران...
تو می‌باری...
تا بوی کاهگل را
که فراموش کرده‌ای
به خاطر آوری.
باران ببار...
زنی را که دوست دارم
سفر می‌کند
و چون برگردد
مرا از خاطر برده است...
تهران، پاییز ۱۳۶۸

===machine===

Hey... rain...
You are raining...
so that you may bring to mind
the smell of straw-and-clay
that you have forgotten.
Rain, rain down...
The woman I love
goes travelling
and when she comes back
she has put me out of mind...
Tehran, autumn 1368

===lantern===

Hey... rain...
you are raining...
so that the smell of adobe
you have let go of
comes back to mind.
Rain, rain down...
The woman I love
is off travelling,
and when she comes back
she has put me out of mind...

Tehran, autumn 1368

